The product's own name, as Android reads it.

This file is small on purpose. It holds only the strings that are proper
nouns — a name is not translated, so it does not belong in the translatable
string catalogue at //taffy/resources/catalog. Everything a person reads
that is a sentence rather than a name lives there instead, is externalized
for translation, and is covered by the pseudo-localization check
(PAR-L10N-001).

A Chromium derivative does not inherit the Chrome name or logo
(chromium/README.md, decision 0001). This file is the replacement, and the
target that carries it is declared with resource overlay precedence so that
it wins over the upstream value of the same resource name rather than
colliding with it.

VERIFY AT SP-01: that `app_name` is still the resource the Chrome Android
manifest's `android:label` resolves, and whether the task switcher and the
site-settings surfaces read a second name resource at the pinned milestone.
Upstream file to read: chrome/android/java/res_chromium/values/strings.xml
and the `android:label` attribute in chrome/android/java/AndroidManifest.xml.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- The launcher and task-switcher label. A brand name, never translated;
         the marks in brand/ spell the wordmark `taffyGo` and repository prose
         spells the product `TaffyGo` (brand/README.md). The platform label
         follows prose, because it sits beside other app names rather than
         beside the mark. -->
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">TaffyGo</string>

    <!-- The home-screen widget labels. Upstream defines all three beside
         app_name in its channel constants, marked non-translatable there
         too, so the overlay must shadow them or the widget picker says
         Chromium. Same substitution mechanism as app_name (decision 0019;
         patch specification 0002 records it); check_shadowed_names.py keeps
         these names in step with upstream. -->
    <string name="bookmark_widget_title" translatable="false">TaffyGo bookmarks</string>
    <string name="search_widget_title" translatable="false">TaffyGo search</string>
    <string name="quick_action_search_widget_title" translatable="false">TaffyGo quick action search</string>
</resources>
